A||||13||CHARLIE FERGUSON||se to gt conversion||||5||
Z||000000||CHARLIE FERGUSON||02-03-2001||11:03 AM||||i want to take the aero kit off my gt and put it on the se. the gt is in rough shape interior wise. the se is in great shape,  both cars run good. the gt is auto and se is 4 spd.what would you guys suggest, and is it difficult to move all the body parts to the se?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mattsfiero||02-03-2001||11:53 AM||||Well Charlie I have seen one other member make the change from SE to GT before. The Body panels on any fiero will attach to yours however in order to change the rear notch back to the fast back will require changing the tail lights, Deck Lid, and the sailpanel. Aigning them may be a little tricky at first but it can be done. <P>------------------<BR>Matt<BR>85 custom coupe<BR>Mattsfiero@aol.com<BR>www.anglefire.com/ma3/mattsfiero||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||02-03-2001||12:28 PM||||Depends on what year model the cars are too. Notchback to notchback is a breeze. Aero to nothcback is a little more involved. In addition to what is listed above I think you also have to change the rear wiring harness, the impact absorbers front and rear and possibly even the rear inner fender wells. Does that sound right to anyone that has done this?<P>Basically, it can be done without a lot of fabrication. Just be prepared to go deep enough into the car to do it... It is more than just body panels.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||MR86GT||02-03-2001||01:07 PM||||you don't have to change the inner wheel wells, but you do have to change the trunk gasket which more than likely will tear upon removal. but all in all an easy swap.<P><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||02-03-2001||01:39 PM||||What years SE and GT?  (Do you want to swap fascias and ground effects panels, or a fastback?)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||MontanaFiero||02-03-2001||02:48 PM||||Don't forget the TRIM. The SE trim is GROOVED, and the GT FASTBACK trim is most likey ROUND. This will involve changing the front FACIA as well, because the trim is molded with the facia.<P>Brian||||reg||2
Z||000006||strick8||02-05-2001||10:00 AM||||This link shows you how to do Notchback to Fastback with great pics. <A HREF="http://fiero.net/showroom/fastback.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fiero.net/showroom/fastback.html</A> ||||reg||10
