Z||000010||MrPBody||02-05-2001||08:58 PM||||I have installed an '87 coupe fascia on my '85 SE.  That's not exactly what you're doing, but similar.<P>I <B>THINK</B> you will need to change -- in addition to the fascias -- the impact absorbing "waffle" under the fascia (at least front, maybe rear), wheel well liners, air dam, maybe a few panels or shrouds under the front fascia, and the side ground effects molding.  And maybe something about the front turn signals if they don't align with new fascia openings.  I don't think you need to change any wiring.<P>I think ground effects attach through holes in fenders, quarters, and door skin, so you may need to cut new holes or transplant body panels from the GT.  Rocker panels attach by rivets, and tabs into the fenders and quarters.  I think ground effects molding attaches with molding clips like upper door molding.  If so, you'll need new clips; they almost always break.<P>There should be more information about this in past posts.  Good luck!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||jch82||02-06-2001||12:09 PM||||So everything (bumpers, ground effects, etc.) pretty much bolts right up to the 85SE? Except for maybe the rivet holes that need to be drilled.<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Before you criticize someone, walk a mile in his shoes. That way, if he  gets angry, he'll be a mile way - and barefoot....||||reg||5
Z||000012||MrPBody||02-06-2001||08:22 PM||||As far as I know, yes.  I think it's a common swap.  If I were doing it, I would lean toward swapping body panels rather than cutting new mounting holes.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||stimpy||02-07-2001||01:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sqoach:<BR><B> fiero show in oklahoma??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> point me in that direction!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>FYI on the Fiero Show. It should be coming up 2nd weekend in May. I will be attending the next club meeting this Sunday and will post a thread giving some info...  I truely and sincerely hope that everyone within driving distance can make the scene. Last year I had the opportunity to meet some really cool folks from Texas (pollock, where you at?) with some very nice cars. Unfortunately the turnout was a bit slim. Y'all be there, ok?||||reg||1
